DATA ATTRIBUTION (FIRST RELEASE)

The public build of Open Granth is rendered from a
corpus derived from the Shabad OS database
(https://github.com/shabados/database).

The first release of Open Granth includes:

  - Gurmukhi text and metadata imported from Shabad OS data
  - Romanized transliteration generated locally by Open Granth
  - English translation imported from the DSSK translation asset
    in the Shabad OS database, attributed there to Dr. Sant S.
    Khalsa, publication date 2013-03

The English layer is an imported study aid. It is not
Open Granth's own interpretation.
Within Open Granth, the Gurmukhi is the source layer;
the Roman and English layers are reading aids.

Open Granth does not claim copyright over Gurbani text
or third-party translation text included from upstream sources.

SCOPE

The first release provides:
  - Gurmukhi corpus (all 1,430 angs)
  - Romanized transliteration
  - DSSK English translation for study
  - Static browsable site
  - Verification tool (citation-first)
  - MCP server for AI clients

The first release does not provide:
  - AI-generated interpretation presented as authoritative
  - Any claim of religious or scholarly authority

Open Granth does not claim religious, scholarly, or
interpretive authority.

